G8009.definition:
1. adulterated, spurious, base , of coin, (Theognis Elegiacus) 
2. metaphorically base, false, spurious, fraudulent , of men, (Theognis Elegiacus); of oracles, deceitful , (Herdotus Historicus); ἐν κιβδήλῳ (Euripides) 
from κίβδος (ML)

G8190.definition:
1. a band of robbers , (Xenophon Historicus):—; a retreat  or nest of robbers , (Strabo Geographus) 
2. robbery , in plural, (Lucian) 
from λῃστής (ML)

G8623.definition:
1. alternation, alternating motion , τῶν σκελῶν (Plutarch) 
2. a change for the worse, alteration , (Plato Philosophus) 
from παραλλάσσω (ML)

G8640.definition:
1. a placing in line of battle , ἐκ παρατάξεως in regular battle , (Thucydides), etc. 
2. of marshalling  a political party, arrangement , (Aeschines Orator) 
from παρατάσσω (ML)

G8679.definition:
1. φόνια πειρατήρια the murderous ordeal , (Euripides) 
2. a pirate's nest , (Strabo Geographus) 
from πειρα_τής (ML)
